  "title": "A New Look For The Eth Link",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Main article",
      "text": "Two buses run back and forth between ETH Zurich’s Zentrum and Hönggerberg campuses on every weekday, making a total of 69 trips per day. These vehicles have now been given a makeover.\n\nOne of the buses has been sporting the new design since 26 May, with the second due to follow in mid-June. The ETH Link is run by Eurobus and transports almost 2,000 people on an average day."
    }
